Well, this doesn't have to be too complicated.  Let's see.

Polypiling on an altar, around level 4 (OK, so this is a recognized
sin, but I was just foolin' around).  Since I was of low level I was
doing the old poly-pet routine as well as transforming the contents of
a very large shop.

So anyway, my last legit zap had left me with a cave spider as a pet.
Let me tell you, cave spiders make durn poor pets.  For one thing,
half the time they're hiding under something and you don't even know
where they are.  For another, they don't go anywhere!  This guy just
sat on the altar for rounds and rounds - I would try to move, and
then get the message "You stop to avoid hitting your cave spider" but
there was no choice but to wait until it moved of its own accord.

Here I am, trying to set off my last zap - only takes me 20 or 30
tries.  And what happens?  Nothing.  No polys at all.  At first I
thought it was only the pet, but nothing else changed either.  I guess
this drives home the evils of polypiling.  Perhaps if I had been on a
co-aligned altar ... :-)

Allen


